    "text": "Two particles of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>M are&nbsp;</mi></math>moving with speeds of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, as shown in the figure. They collide at the origin and after that they move along the indicated directions with speeds <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math> and <math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>, respectively. The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are, nearly<br /><br><br /><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c9f6b946-3b16-4bbf-8a45-e0be90fb396b-image9.png\" />",
